Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 18:36:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02646/11362] [outer-loop] Config Layer B breadth sweep: tn36
 also GROUNDS (Tier 2) -- scaffold generalizes beyond ka59

Swept the scaffolded LLM rule-inducer across the config-class games. Result: 2 of the groundable config
games now reach Tier 2 GROUNDED RELATIONAL rules -- ka59 (prior) AND tn36 (fires_on_win=True, fpr=0.0
over 6 non-wins). The structured-extraction scaffold GENERALIZES; it is not a ka59 one-off.

Per game: tn36 TIER2_GROUNDED_RELATIONAL; sc25 BLOCKED (generic banked-replay does not reproduce its win
-- needs the adapter's warmup/fresh_env handling); cd82/wa30 TIER0_FAIL (no coherent predicate); the
no-banked-solve games (bp35/dc22/g50t/lf52/s5i5) error in collect() because there is no ground-truth win
to verify against (they cannot be grounded regardless -- a robustness gap, not a missed win).

Bottom line: the config win-rule wall is now demonstrably crackable with the local offline model on the
count/relation class (2 grounded), loads the 12B once and reuses the server across games. Adversarial-verify clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
